    "function": "read_doc",
    "issue": "Broken access control: the user/owner argument is ignored, so any caller can fetch a document's title by id regardless of who owns it.",
    "reproduction": "repro.py repro_idor(): service.read_doc(db, 'bob', 1) returns ('public',) — bob reads alice's document — while on a correct service the owner mismatch must yield None."
  },
  {
    "function": "read_export",
    "issue": "Path traversal via string prefix matching: containment uses str(target).startswith(str(root)), so a sibling path whose name shares the root's prefix (e.g. ../exports_evil) is treated as inside root and read.",
    "reproduction": "repro.py repro_path_traversal(): with root <tmp>/exports and a sibling <tmp>/exports_evil/secret.txt containing TOP-SECRET, read_export(root, '../exports_evil/secret.txt') returns TOP-SECRET because <tmp>/exports_evil satisfies the startswith(<tmp>/exports) check."
  }
]

